summary:
As the largest single-district community college system in the nation, Maricopa Community Colleges educates more Arizona residents than its three large public universities combined.&nbsp;
The system operates 10 main campuses across the Phoenix metropolitan area and more than 30 satellite sites, serving nearly 100,000 students and employing 14,000 faculty members and staff in the 2026 spring semester.&nbsp;
Those superlatives and numbers are all familiar to Jamie Spradlin, MCC’s CISO. When he took his position in June 2024, his first order of business was to establish a cybersecurity program…
